======================================================================
2. Code adapted into this repository
======================================================================

src/engine/astro.ts, src/engine/satellites.ts, src/engine/realSky.ts, src/engine/nightSky.ts
  Ported from Lumbridge's earlier Tera prototype (solar, moon, satellites, Starlink, night
  lights), now released under Apache-2.0 as part of Lumbridge Tera. Astronomical formulas
  after Jean Meeus, "Astronomical Algorithms" (2nd ed., 1998) and the NOAA Solar Calculator;
  planet elements after Paul Schlyter, "How to compute planetary positions" (public text);
  star colours from black-body temperatures (Ballesteros 2012 and Tanner Helland's RGB fit).

src/engine/skyModel.ts
  The Preetham sky model is ported from the shader of three.js's Sky addon
  (examples/jsm/objects/Sky.js).
  Copyright © 2010-2026 three.js authors. Licence: MIT (text below).

workers/server/tera_worker/splat.py
  The .spz encoding follows the format of nianticlabs/spz (https://github.com/nianticlabs/spz),
  Copyright (c) 2024 Niantic, Inc. Licence: MIT. Written independently; no source copied.

workers/docker/kimodo/arm64/tera_simd_arm64.h
  Includes sse2neon.h (https://github.com/DLTcollab/sse2neon, MIT) at image build time;
  sse2neon itself is not in this repository.

workers/docker/*
  The Dockerfiles download and patch upstream projects at build time (NVIDIA Lyra,
  Kimodo, Microsoft TRELLIS.2, MoGe, gsplat, mamba, causal-conv1d, CuMesh, FlexGEMM,
  utils3d and others). None of that code is in this repository; each keeps its own
  licence. Model weights are never in this repository: see workers/README.md for every
  model and its licence.

